 "transcript": {
  "answer": "No. The Aussie is fairly strong against the yen right now, though it has slipped from its recent peak.\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 buys about ¥109.67 (October 2026 data to date).\n- **Over the past year:** It's up about 9%, from ¥100.84 in October 2025.\n- **Peak:** It reached about ¥114.28 in April 2026 and ¥114.54 in August. That's roughly 4% above today's level.\n- **Recent drop:** It fell from ¥114.54 at the end of August to ¥109.47 at the end of September. It has been flat since.\n\nThe Aussie is also holding up against other currencies. The trade-weighted index is 64.4, up from 61.2 a year ago but below its 66.6 high in May. AUD/USD is about 0.695, up from 0.655 a year ago.\n\nSo the yen is weaker than a year ago, and the Aussie has eased a little from its highs. It's not weak by the standards of the past year.",
